# No em dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`) anywhere in this project: UI copy, comments, docs, commits, metadata, OG text, tweets, store listings.

Also never fake them with spaced hyphens (` - `) or en dashes (`–`) as sentence punctuation. For number ranges, use a plain hyphen (`0-100`).

## Prefer instead

- Commas, periods, or semicolons
- Parentheses for asides
- Colons for short labels
- A plain hyphen only for compounds or numeric ranges (`tip-foam`, `0-100`)

```text
❌ A quiet place to watch — live dials
❌ A quiet place to watch - live dials
✅ A quiet place to watch: live dials
✅ A quiet place to watch. Live dials.
✅ A quiet place to watch (live dials)
```

If you see an existing em dash (or spaced-hyphen aside) while editing a file, replace it.
